# Production build values. Vite loads .env.production ON TOP OF .env for a
# `vite build`, so this overrides the localhost value in .env — which is a
# DEV convenience and must never reach a production bundle.
#
# Empty = same-origin: the app calls /api/... relative, and nginx proxies
# those to the backend container (whatsapp-dashboard/nginx.conf).
#
# This file exists because .env's localhost:3000 was being compiled into the
# production image: every visitor's browser then called their OWN machine, so
# the dashboard showed no data (Pipeline/Chats empty) even though the server
# and database were perfectly healthy. The AI chatbot kept working throughout
# because it is server-side and never involves the browser.
VITE_BACKEND_URL=
